Wrapper calss:
 A wrapper class in java is used to convert primitive data types into objects.
 Java provides one wrapper class for each primitive type.
 
Why wrapper nclasses are needed?
-Java wroks with objects not primitives in many places like collections , generics,etc.
-Wrapper classes allow primitives to be treated as objects.
-Provide utility methods for type conversion
-Support null values (primitives cannot)

Primitive datatupe ->Wrapper calss
byte ---------------calss Byte
short---------------class Short
int-----------------class Integer
long----------------class Long
float---------------class Float
double -------------class Double
char----------------class Character
boolean-------------class Boolean

